1
00:00:04,120 --> 00:00:06,380
Hey, guys.

2
00:00:04,120 --> 00:00:06,380
Hey.

3
00:00:06,540 --> 00:00:09,800
So, what do you think?

4
00:00:11,050 --> 00:00:12,260
About what?

5
00:00:11,050 --> 00:00:12,260
What?

6
00:00:13,340 --> 00:00:16,890
Are you kidding? Okay, I'll give you a hint. I'll give you a hint.

7
00:00:19,680 --> 00:00:22,770
Eyes. No, no. Your eyes! No.

8
00:00:22,930 --> 00:00:24,520
Chandler's eyes!

9
00:00:25,730 --> 00:00:27,440
I got glasses.

10
00:00:27,650 --> 00:00:30,070
You always had glasses.

11
00:00:32,900 --> 00:00:34,450
No, I didn't.

12
00:00:35,820 --> 00:00:37,240
Are you sure?

13
00:00:38,780 --> 00:00:40,330
Didn't you used to have a pair?

14
00:00:40,490 --> 00:00:44,660
They were really round and burgundy, and they made you look kind of, um...

15
00:00:44,830 --> 00:00:46,870
Feminine.

16
00:00:44,830 --> 00:00:46,870
Yes!

17
00:00:47,250 --> 00:00:48,290
No.

18
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:51,340
I think the glasses look great. They make you look sexy.

19
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:53,010
Really?

20
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:53,010
Yeah.

21
00:00:53,170 --> 00:00:55,380
You didn't think I used to wear glasses, right?

22
00:00:55,550 --> 00:00:56,590
Of course.

23
00:00:55,550 --> 00:00:56,590
Pfft.

24
00:00:56,760 --> 00:00:58,260
I had no idea.

25
00:01:53,860 --> 00:01:55,940
What do you want for an engagement present?

26
00:01:56,110 --> 00:01:58,240
Oh, that's okay, we're not having a party...

27
00:01:58,400 --> 00:02:01,200
...so you don't have to get us...

28
00:01:58,400 --> 00:02:01,200
Ah, buh-buh-buh! Heh.

29
00:02:01,370 --> 00:02:05,450
If someone wants to give us a present, we don't want to deprive them of that joy.

30
00:02:06,450 --> 00:02:08,960
Oh, you should get them one of those little CD players.

31
00:02:09,170 --> 00:02:10,500
Oh, I already have one.

32
00:02:10,670 --> 00:02:13,880
Unless someone borrowed it and left it at the gynecologist.

33
00:02:17,090 --> 00:02:20,550
Yeah, and by "someone" she means Joey.

34
00:02:21,970 --> 00:02:23,350
Hey, I know what I want!

35
00:02:23,510 --> 00:02:26,310
What we want, honey.

36
00:02:23,510 --> 00:02:26,310
No, you don't want this.

37
00:02:27,310 --> 00:02:29,980
I want to have your grandmother's cookie recipe.

38
00:02:30,190 --> 00:02:32,600
You mean the chocolate chip cookie recipe?

39
00:02:32,770 --> 00:02:34,610
Uh-huh, yeah.

40
00:02:32,770 --> 00:02:34,610
The one my grandmother...

41
00:02:34,770 --> 00:02:36,440
...made me swear on her deathbed...

42
00:02:36,610 --> 00:02:39,070
...that I would never let out of our family?

43
00:02:39,820 --> 00:02:42,870
Dying people say the craziest things.

44
00:02:44,410 --> 00:02:47,830
I've wanted it for years. I was gonna make cookies for my children.

45
00:02:48,910 --> 00:02:51,500
Break my heart. Oh, all right.

46
00:02:51,710 --> 00:02:55,210
I'll be the mom who makes the world's best chocolate chip cookies.

47
00:02:55,460 --> 00:02:58,710
Our kids are gonna be fat, aren't they?

48
00:03:00,720 --> 00:03:02,260
Ahoy!

49
00:03:00,720 --> 00:03:02,260
Hey.

50
00:03:02,470 --> 00:03:05,180
How's the boat?

51
00:03:02,470 --> 00:03:05,180
I'm getting into this sailing stuff.

52
00:03:05,350 --> 00:03:07,180
You finally took it out of the marina?

53
00:03:07,810 --> 00:03:09,270
Why would I do that?

54
00:03:09,980 --> 00:03:12,850
It took three guys to get the thing in there.

55
00:03:13,650 --> 00:03:15,770
If you don't sail it, what do you do on it?

56
00:03:15,980 --> 00:03:17,860
It's a great place to just kind of sit...

57
00:03:18,030 --> 00:03:21,490
...hang around, drink a few beers, eat some chips.

58
00:03:23,030 --> 00:03:26,280
It's good that you finally have a place to do that.

59
00:03:27,080 --> 00:03:29,370
Joey, I could teach you to sail if you want.

60
00:03:29,580 --> 00:03:32,000
You could?

61
00:03:29,580 --> 00:03:32,000
Yeah, I've been sailing my whole life.

62
00:03:32,170 --> 00:03:35,210
When I was 15, my dad bought me my own boat.

63
00:03:36,670 --> 00:03:38,800
Your own boat?

64
00:03:36,670 --> 00:03:38,800
He was trying to cheer me up.

65
00:03:39,010 --> 00:03:40,880
My pony was sick.

66
00:03:52,230 --> 00:03:54,390
You know what I was thinking?

67
00:03:52,230 --> 00:03:54,390
What?

68
00:03:54,850 --> 00:03:56,940
Nothing, I just like to go like this.

69
00:03:58,150 --> 00:04:01,320
Chandler, what are you doing tonight?

70
00:03:58,150 --> 00:04:01,320
Why, do you have a lecture?

71
00:04:01,490 --> 00:04:04,780
No, why?

72
00:04:01,490 --> 00:04:04,780
Then, free as a bird. What's up?

73
00:04:04,950 --> 00:04:07,740
Uh, my dad wants to know if you want to play racquetball.

74
00:04:07,910 --> 00:04:09,620
Wow, that's great! Dad must like you.

75
00:04:09,790 --> 00:04:12,870
He doesn't ask just anyone to play.

76
00:04:09,790 --> 00:04:12,870
He didn't really ask for you.

77
00:04:13,040 --> 00:04:16,540
He asked for "Chauncey." I assumed he meant you.

78
00:04:17,170 --> 00:04:18,630
Did you correct him?

79
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:21,420
No, I thought it would be more fun this way.

80
00:04:22,880 --> 00:04:25,340
Maybe this is something you could do this every week.

81
00:04:25,510 --> 00:04:27,010
Or you could sit on the porch...

82
00:04:27,180 --> 00:04:29,640
...and make sure no one steals the trashcans.

83
00:04:29,810 --> 00:04:31,930
He does that every week too.

84
00:04:33,270 --> 00:04:36,560
Just so you know, you have to let him win. He hates to lose.

85
00:04:36,730 --> 00:04:39,730
Oh, no problem. Maybe I'll play with my left hand.

86
00:04:40,900 --> 00:04:42,190
You're not a lefty?

87
00:04:43,650 --> 00:04:45,360
Does anybody know me?

88
00:04:50,450 --> 00:04:51,490
What's wrong, Phoebe?

89
00:04:51,660 --> 00:04:55,080
I just went to my old apartment to get you the cookie recipe...

90
00:04:55,250 --> 00:04:57,790
...and that stupid fire burned it up!

91
00:04:57,960 --> 00:05:01,880
No! Why didn't you make a copy and keep it in a fireproof box...

92
00:05:02,050 --> 00:05:05,010
...and keep it at least 100 yards away from the original?

93
00:05:10,640 --> 00:05:13,310
Because I'm normal.

94
00:05:15,140 --> 00:05:17,690
That was the one legacy my grandmother left me.

95
00:05:17,940 --> 00:05:20,770
And I know you wanted it as an engagement present.

96
00:05:20,940 --> 00:05:23,110
We have to get you an engagement present?

97
00:05:24,070 --> 00:05:25,320
Don't worry about it.

98
00:05:25,530 --> 00:05:28,070
No one got me an engagement present.

99
00:05:28,450 --> 00:05:32,240
Okay, here. I don't have the recipe, but here.

100
00:05:32,490 --> 00:05:34,910
I wish you health and happiness.

101
00:05:35,870 --> 00:05:37,960
An old cookie?

102
00:05:38,250 --> 00:05:41,590
See, this is what happens when you don't register for gifts.

103
00:05:42,710 --> 00:05:47,420
I made a batch and I froze it. And this is the only one left.

104
00:05:47,590 --> 00:05:50,090
We can't accept this.

105
00:05:47,590 --> 00:05:50,090
Why not?

106
00:05:51,050 --> 00:05:53,100
Because it's gross.

107
00:05:53,810 --> 00:05:57,060
No, wait. I think I can figure out the recipe from this cookie.

108
00:05:57,270 --> 00:05:58,730
I do this at work all the time.

109
00:05:58,900 --> 00:06:00,440
Really?

110
00:05:58,900 --> 00:06:00,440
Yeah, I think I can.

111
00:06:00,610 --> 00:06:01,980
Oh, yay!

112
00:06:05,400 --> 00:06:07,280
Okay, Ross, we owe you a present.

113
00:06:07,450 --> 00:06:09,780
Two! I've been engaged twice.

114
00:06:19,040 --> 00:06:20,290
Look at this clown.

115
00:06:20,460 --> 00:06:23,790
Because he's got a bigger boat he thinks he can take up the whole river.

116
00:06:23,960 --> 00:06:26,670
Get out of the way, jackass!

117
00:06:28,420 --> 00:06:31,050
Who names their boat Coast Guard, anyway?

118
00:06:33,810 --> 00:06:36,810
That is the Coast Guard.

119
00:06:33,810 --> 00:06:36,810
What are they doing out here?

120
00:06:36,970 --> 00:06:39,230
The coast is all the way over there.

121
00:06:40,100 --> 00:06:41,600
Joey, just ignore the boats.

122
00:06:41,770 --> 00:06:44,060
We're not finished with our lesson.

123
00:06:41,770 --> 00:06:44,060
All right.

124
00:06:44,230 --> 00:06:46,480
I'm gonna go over the basic points one more time.

125
00:06:46,650 --> 00:06:49,820
Come on, Rach. Not again. I got it, okay? Let's start sailing!

126
00:06:49,990 --> 00:06:53,620
I want to go over there where that boatload of girls is. Yeah, oh!

127
00:06:54,870 --> 00:06:56,240
Oh, is that what you wanna do?

128
00:06:56,410 --> 00:06:59,160
You want to give a shout out to the old hot chicas?

129
00:06:59,330 --> 00:07:01,670
Okay, let's do that, Sailor Joe.

130
00:07:01,830 --> 00:07:05,000
Quick question, though: What's this called?

131
00:07:05,550 --> 00:07:09,460
Uh, boat rope?

132
00:07:05,550 --> 00:07:09,460
Wrong.

133
00:07:09,630 --> 00:07:12,340
How do you get the mainsail up?

134
00:07:09,630 --> 00:07:12,340
Uh...

135
00:07:12,930 --> 00:07:14,590
Rub it?

136
00:07:17,640 --> 00:07:21,140
No. What do you do if I say we're coming about?

137
00:07:21,310 --> 00:07:23,730
I'd say, "Come again?" Ha, ha.

138
00:07:23,900 --> 00:07:26,440
No, no, I know this one. I know this one. Uh, um...

139
00:07:28,730 --> 00:07:30,530
Time's up. Now you're dead.

140
00:07:30,700 --> 00:07:31,820
And deaf!

141
00:07:31,990 --> 00:07:34,160
Okay, you go on and make your little jokes.

142
00:07:34,320 --> 00:07:36,370
If you don't know what you're doing at sea...

143
00:07:36,530 --> 00:07:39,950
...you will die at sea. Am I getting through to you, sailor?

144
00:07:40,460 --> 00:07:42,460
Yes.

145
00:07:40,460 --> 00:07:42,460
Don't just say yes.

146
00:07:42,620 --> 00:07:45,170
This isn't a game. You could get hurt out here!

147
00:07:45,330 --> 00:07:48,130
So do you want to pay attention, or do you want to die?

148
00:07:51,510 --> 00:07:54,260
I want to make a ship-to-shore call to Chandler.

149
00:08:03,730 --> 00:08:06,520
All right, I definitely taste nutmeg.

150
00:08:03,730 --> 00:08:06,520
You do?

151
00:08:06,690 --> 00:08:09,520
You don't? Heh. Well, that's the difference...

152
00:08:09,690 --> 00:08:11,530
...between a professional and a layman.

153
00:08:13,240 --> 00:08:14,950
That and arrogance.

154
00:08:17,120 --> 00:08:18,160
Hey.

155
00:08:18,370 --> 00:08:19,910
Hey. How was sailing?

156
00:08:20,620 --> 00:08:22,620
I don't want to talk about it.

157
00:08:23,290 --> 00:08:25,250
You could've saved me a whole cookie.

158
00:08:23,290 --> 00:08:25,250
No!

159
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:31,590
Women are mean!

160
00:08:36,340 --> 00:08:37,550
I can't believe that.

161
00:08:37,720 --> 00:08:41,060
Now the only thing left of my grandmother's legacy is...

162
00:08:41,220 --> 00:08:42,890
...this crumb.

163
00:08:44,810 --> 00:08:47,690
I wish you a long and happy marriage.

164
00:08:50,780 --> 00:08:52,570
Hey.

165
00:08:50,780 --> 00:08:52,570
How was it?

166
00:08:52,780 --> 00:08:54,440
Well, I had a great time.

167
00:08:54,610 --> 00:08:57,950
Um, Chauncey on the other hand...

168
00:08:58,160 --> 00:09:00,160
I will tell the story.

169
00:09:00,410 --> 00:09:03,500
It was going great. I let him win, we were bonding...

170
00:09:03,750 --> 00:09:05,580
...he even said I could call him Dad.

171
00:09:05,750 --> 00:09:07,580
And what did he ask you not to call him?

172
00:09:08,540 --> 00:09:10,000
"Daddy."

173
00:09:11,170 --> 00:09:13,130
Look, here's the story.

174
00:09:14,010 --> 00:09:16,420
We had just finished playing racquetball...

175
00:09:16,590 --> 00:09:18,220
...and we were gonna take a steam.

176
00:09:18,390 --> 00:09:19,970
I walk into the steam room...

177
00:09:20,140 --> 00:09:22,060
...and it's really steamy.

178
00:09:24,640 --> 00:09:27,810
So I take off my glasses, and that's when it happened.

179
00:09:27,980 --> 00:09:29,020
Guys?

180
00:09:29,190 --> 00:09:32,190
Over here.

181
00:09:29,190 --> 00:09:32,190
Have a seat, son.

182
00:09:37,570 --> 00:09:39,360
Hey!

183
00:09:49,380 --> 00:09:52,380
Oh, my God, Chandler! I can't believe it.

184
00:09:49,380 --> 00:09:52,380
I know.

185
00:09:52,550 --> 00:09:54,960
You gave my father a lap dance.

186
00:09:58,430 --> 00:10:00,970
Why do they put so much steam in there?

187
00:10:02,510 --> 00:10:07,270
Because otherwise they'd have to call it the "room" room.

188
00:10:08,770 --> 00:10:12,860
Why, okay? Why? Why did that have to happen?

189
00:10:13,650 --> 00:10:15,280
Come on, it's not that big a deal.

190
00:10:15,480 --> 00:10:17,860
Not that big a deal? There...

191
00:10:18,110 --> 00:10:20,490
There was touching of things.

192
00:10:20,700 --> 00:10:22,870
I know you wanted to bond with my dad...

193
00:10:23,080 --> 00:10:26,240
...but did you have to bond to that part?

194
00:10:29,540 --> 00:10:33,080
Listen, I'm sure Dad doesn't care. He probably thought this was funny.

195
00:10:33,250 --> 00:10:35,050
He'll be telling this story for years.

196
00:10:35,210 --> 00:10:38,010
I don't want him to tell this story for years.

197
00:10:38,300 --> 00:10:40,590
Oh, but he will.

198
00:10:41,430 --> 00:10:45,510
He still tells the story about how Monica tried to escape from fat camp.

199
00:10:47,350 --> 00:10:48,480
I wasn't escaping.

200
00:10:48,680 --> 00:10:50,940
Then how'd you get caught in the barbed wire?

201
00:10:52,100 --> 00:10:53,810
I was trying to help out a squirrel.

202
00:10:54,020 --> 00:10:55,820
You were trying to eat it.

203
00:10:59,450 --> 00:11:01,990
If that is your father calling to tell this story...

204
00:11:02,200 --> 00:11:03,950
...then the marriage is off!

205
00:11:04,450 --> 00:11:06,530
Come on. Hello.

206
00:11:07,240 --> 00:11:09,580
I'm sorry, you have the wrong number.

207
00:11:09,750 --> 00:11:11,750
Okay, I'll call you later, Dad. I love you.

208
00:11:18,460 --> 00:11:20,630
All right, I'm off to see your dad.

209
00:11:18,460 --> 00:11:20,630
Oh, whoa.

210
00:11:20,840 --> 00:11:23,010
Aren't you a little overdressed?

211
00:11:24,220 --> 00:11:27,720
Yeah, and you better make sure he tips you this time.

212
00:11:28,810 --> 00:11:32,100
I figured I would try to convince him not to tell the story anymore...

213
00:11:32,350 --> 00:11:35,230
...and I figured the best way to do that was face to face.

214
00:11:35,480 --> 00:11:37,980
And by "face," I don't mean his lap.

215
00:11:38,230 --> 00:11:41,070
And by "face," I don't mean my ass.

216
00:11:43,860 --> 00:11:46,660
Are you getting Monica and Chandler an engagement present?

217
00:11:46,870 --> 00:11:49,240
I don't know. You know, they didn't get us anything.

218
00:11:49,450 --> 00:11:51,080
Thank you!

219
00:11:53,120 --> 00:11:54,210
Hey.

220
00:11:53,120 --> 00:11:54,210
Hey.

221
00:11:54,710 --> 00:11:55,960
Well, hello.

222
00:11:56,170 --> 00:11:59,050
So when are we getting back out on the water, matey?

223
00:11:59,550 --> 00:12:03,470
Oh, uh, I don't know the boat way to say this, but, never.

224
00:12:05,760 --> 00:12:09,060
Why not?

225
00:12:05,760 --> 00:12:09,060
Because you're mean on the boat.

226
00:12:09,220 --> 00:12:11,520
Wha...? I was just trying to teach you.

227
00:12:11,680 --> 00:12:14,100
Well, lesson learned. Rachel is mean.

228
00:12:15,060 --> 00:12:18,190
Yep, yep, yep, yep, yep, yep.

229
00:12:19,280 --> 00:12:21,570
I remember when she took me out on her dad's boat.

230
00:12:21,740 --> 00:12:23,570
She wouldn't let me help out at all.

231
00:12:23,780 --> 00:12:27,160
Excuse me, I wanted you to help. But you couldn't move your arms...

232
00:12:27,410 --> 00:12:30,370
...because you were wearing three life jackets.

233
00:12:31,620 --> 00:12:34,460
You have to respect the sea.

234
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:38,790
Look, Joey, I'm sorry if you thought that was mean.

235
00:12:38,960 --> 00:12:41,130
But I tell you something, that was not mean.

236
00:12:41,300 --> 00:12:45,090
My father is mean. He used to yell at me all the time on the boat.

237
00:12:45,340 --> 00:12:48,430
It was horrible. I was being a really good teacher.

238
00:12:48,640 --> 00:12:51,510
Does a good teacher say, "Put down the beer, pinhead!"

239
00:12:52,270 --> 00:12:55,770
Does a good student drink 7 beers during his first lesson?

240
00:12:56,310 --> 00:12:57,520
Six and a half.

241
00:12:58,060 --> 00:13:00,020
You knocked that last one out of my hand.

242
00:13:00,230 --> 00:13:02,150
I didn't want you to get hit by the boom.

243
00:13:02,360 --> 00:13:03,690
Well, it hit me anyway.

244
00:13:03,940 --> 00:13:07,110
It would have hurt a lot less if I had finished that last beer.

245
00:13:08,120 --> 00:13:13,240
I'm sorry. I will try to tone it down and, uh, stop yelling.

246
00:13:13,950 --> 00:13:16,540
You won't boss me around?

247
00:13:13,950 --> 00:13:16,540
I won't boss you around.

248
00:13:16,710 --> 00:13:18,330
And you'll be nice?

249
00:13:16,710 --> 00:13:18,330
I'll be nice.

250
00:13:18,500 --> 00:13:21,210
And you'll be topless?

251
00:13:18,500 --> 00:13:21,210
And I... Joey!

252
00:13:21,380 --> 00:13:22,800
You want me to learn?

253
00:13:27,220 --> 00:13:30,260
Okay, here's batch 22.

254
00:13:30,430 --> 00:13:32,470
Maybe these'll taste like your grandmother's.

255
00:13:32,640 --> 00:13:35,390
This has a bit of orange peel, but no nutmeg.

256
00:13:35,560 --> 00:13:37,480
Mm. Let's give it a shot.

257
00:13:35,560 --> 00:13:37,480
Ugh.

258
00:13:37,690 --> 00:13:40,190
I have not made so many cookies since 9th grade.

259
00:13:40,400 --> 00:13:44,110
What was that for, a bake sale?

260
00:13:40,400 --> 00:13:44,110
No, just a Friday night.

261
00:13:48,660 --> 00:13:50,570
Mm. These are pretty good.

262
00:13:50,740 --> 00:13:53,200
Yeah, but not as good as batch 17.

263
00:13:50,740 --> 00:13:53,200
Mm-mm.

264
00:13:53,410 --> 00:13:54,450
Which one was that?

265
00:13:54,620 --> 00:13:56,790
The ones we had after you almost threw up.

266
00:13:57,830 --> 00:14:00,420
Oh, yeah, batch 17 was good.

267
00:14:00,580 --> 00:14:03,290
I did not like batch 16.

268
00:14:04,800 --> 00:14:06,420
I'm okay.

269
00:14:07,590 --> 00:14:10,680
Are there any more from the good batch? We could work off those.

270
00:14:10,850 --> 00:14:14,560
Well, yeah, I think there's one from batch 17 left. Uh...

271
00:14:18,980 --> 00:14:22,480
Batch 16. Sixteen, people, get out of the way!

272
00:14:29,860 --> 00:14:33,740
Okay, Joey. Honey, you're doing really good.

273
00:14:33,950 --> 00:14:37,080
I just need you to step to the portside.

274
00:14:41,460 --> 00:14:43,960
Remember how we talked about the portside?

275
00:14:44,170 --> 00:14:45,710
Oh, yeah.

276
00:14:44,170 --> 00:14:45,710
Right?

277
00:14:45,920 --> 00:14:47,090
No.

278
00:14:48,720 --> 00:14:52,470
It's left, sweetie, but that's okay. That's a tough one.

279
00:14:52,680 --> 00:14:54,100
Why not just say left?

280
00:14:54,310 --> 00:14:56,060
Okay, go to the left.

281
00:15:00,690 --> 00:15:02,230
Ahem, the left.

282
00:15:02,400 --> 00:15:03,650
Huh?

283
00:15:02,400 --> 00:15:03,650
Just sit over there!

284
00:15:03,810 --> 00:15:06,070
Okay! Okay! You're yelling again. See that?

285
00:15:06,230 --> 00:15:10,190
Oh, no, no. Very quiet. Said with love, no yelling.

286
00:15:12,490 --> 00:15:13,740
You know what?

287
00:15:13,910 --> 00:15:17,330
Since I'm here, I'm gonna have a beer on the portside.

288
00:15:18,660 --> 00:15:20,330
See what I did there? Ha, ha.

289
00:15:24,170 --> 00:15:27,130
We're luffing a little. Will you tighten up the Cunningham?

290
00:15:27,710 --> 00:15:31,470
Whoa, you just said a bunch of stuff I don't know.

291
00:15:31,630 --> 00:15:34,390
Joey, come on! We just went over this.

292
00:15:34,550 --> 00:15:38,770
Oh, when we did that was when that bird was overhead with the fish in his mouth.

293
00:15:39,020 --> 00:15:42,020
Did you see it? It was gross.

294
00:15:39,020 --> 00:15:42,020
No! I did not see the bird.

295
00:15:42,190 --> 00:15:46,310
I did not see the fish! I did not see the piece of Styrofoam shaped like Mike Tyson!

296
00:15:47,610 --> 00:15:51,900
I did not, because I was trying to teach you how to sail a boat.

297
00:15:52,070 --> 00:15:54,860
Which obviously is an impossible thing to do.

298
00:15:55,030 --> 00:15:58,160
That's it! You're yelling, and I don't see you taking your top off.

299
00:15:58,330 --> 00:16:00,160
I quit!

300
00:16:00,750 --> 00:16:03,330
What do you mean? You can't quit.

301
00:16:00,750 --> 00:16:03,330
Why not?

302
00:16:03,500 --> 00:16:07,040
Because you're not finished! I won't have it. Greens do not quit.

303
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:09,630
Greens?

304
00:16:10,010 --> 00:16:12,970
I'm a Tribbiani. Tribbianis quit.

305
00:16:16,300 --> 00:16:17,390
Oh, my God. Wait.

306
00:16:17,550 --> 00:16:20,680
Did I...? I just said, "Greens don't quit," didn't I?

307
00:16:20,890 --> 00:16:25,520
Did I say, "Greens don't quit"?

308
00:16:20,890 --> 00:16:25,520
Yes! And you're still yelling at me.

309
00:16:25,690 --> 00:16:28,610
No, I'm not yelling at you. I'm just yelling near you.

310
00:16:28,820 --> 00:16:30,690
Oh, God, Joey. Oh, I'm my father.

311
00:16:30,940 --> 00:16:33,610
Oh, my God. This is horrible.

312
00:16:34,740 --> 00:16:38,620
I've been trying so hard not to be my mother, I did not see this coming.

313
00:16:40,240 --> 00:16:41,830
Ugh, Joey.

314
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:46,870
I'm sorry, I'm so sorry. I just wanted you to learn.

315
00:16:48,590 --> 00:16:50,920
Ugh.

316
00:16:48,590 --> 00:16:50,920
Hey, I...

317
00:16:51,090 --> 00:16:52,670
I did learn.

318
00:16:52,840 --> 00:16:54,970
Really?

319
00:16:52,840 --> 00:16:54,970
Yeah, come on.

320
00:16:55,130 --> 00:16:58,010
No.

321
00:16:55,130 --> 00:16:58,010
Yeah. It's okay.

322
00:16:58,220 --> 00:17:00,640
I know what a mainsail is. Huh?

323
00:17:00,810 --> 00:17:04,730
I know to duck when the boom comes across.

324
00:17:06,440 --> 00:17:08,020
I know port is right.

325
00:17:06,440 --> 00:17:08,020
Left.

326
00:17:08,230 --> 00:17:09,730
Damn it!

327
00:17:12,780 --> 00:17:15,240
You know, I bet it would make my grandma happy...

328
00:17:15,450 --> 00:17:18,360
...to know that we're trying to figure out her recipe.

329
00:17:18,620 --> 00:17:23,080
I bet she's looking up at us and smiling right now.

330
00:17:24,660 --> 00:17:26,500
Looking up?

331
00:17:26,670 --> 00:17:31,290
Oh, yeah, no, she was really nice to me but she's in hell for sure.

332
00:17:33,170 --> 00:17:35,130
Well, I've tried everything. I give up.

333
00:17:35,300 --> 00:17:38,180
I'm not gonna be the mom who makes the world's best cookies.

334
00:17:38,760 --> 00:17:43,600
I do make the best duck confit with broccoli raab.

335
00:17:43,850 --> 00:17:45,020
Kids love that, right?

336
00:17:46,980 --> 00:17:50,560
Aw, Pheeb, isn't there any relative that would have the recipe?

337
00:17:50,730 --> 00:17:52,400
What about your sister?

338
00:17:52,610 --> 00:17:55,440
Oh, no. I made a promise to myself that the next time...

339
00:17:55,650 --> 00:17:58,780
...I would talk to Ursula is over my dead body.

340
00:18:00,200 --> 00:18:04,790
And that's not happening until October 15, 2032.

341
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:07,160
That's the day you're gonna die? See.

342
00:18:07,330 --> 00:18:10,330
Darn it, I've got shuffleboard that day. Heh.

343
00:18:11,250 --> 00:18:13,210
That's what you think.

344
00:18:16,880 --> 00:18:19,840
What about friends of your grandmother? Would they have the recipe?

345
00:18:20,010 --> 00:18:23,600
You know, I may have relatives in France who would know.

346
00:18:23,760 --> 00:18:25,600
My grandmother said she got the recipe...

347
00:18:25,770 --> 00:18:29,350
...from her grandmother, "Nestley Toulouse."

348
00:18:31,230 --> 00:18:32,270
What was her name?

349
00:18:33,020 --> 00:18:36,280
Nestley Toulouse.

350
00:18:37,490 --> 00:18:39,860
Nestley Toulouse?

351
00:18:43,240 --> 00:18:44,910
Ugh.

352
00:18:45,200 --> 00:18:47,790
You Americans always butcher the French language.

353
00:18:49,750 --> 00:18:52,250
Phoebe, is this the recipe?

354
00:18:54,750 --> 00:18:56,130
Yes!

355
00:18:59,260 --> 00:19:00,420
Oh.

356
00:19:01,010 --> 00:19:04,930
I cannot believe that I spent the last two days trying to figure out that recipe.

357
00:19:05,100 --> 00:19:06,810
It was in my cupboard the whole time!

358
00:19:06,970 --> 00:19:10,940
I know! You see, it is stuff like this...

359
00:19:11,100 --> 00:19:13,650
...which is why you're burning in hell!

360
00:19:17,780 --> 00:19:19,030
So you understand.

361
00:19:19,190 --> 00:19:21,900
I'd feel more comfortable if you didn't tell people.

362
00:19:22,070 --> 00:19:24,740
You know, I'm a little embarrassed about it.

363
00:19:24,910 --> 00:19:28,290
I understand completely. There's nothing more horrifying...

364
00:19:28,450 --> 00:19:30,960
...than embarrassing yourself in front of your in-laws.

365
00:19:31,120 --> 00:19:35,500
As a matter of fact, when I started dating Judy, I was unemployed.

366
00:19:35,670 --> 00:19:37,710
Her father asked me what I did for a living.

367
00:19:37,880 --> 00:19:40,090
I told him I was a lawyer.

368
00:19:40,260 --> 00:19:42,680
     What'd you do when they found out?

369
00:19:40,260 --> 00:19:42,680
They never did.

370
00:19:42,840 --> 00:19:46,550
So if you ever see me giving them legal advice, just nod along.

371
00:19:48,060 --> 00:19:49,310
Shall we?

372
00:20:04,410 --> 00:20:07,370
So, I guess we wear swimsuits in here.

373
00:20:19,590 --> 00:20:22,840
Well, Joey, I hate to admit it...

374
00:20:23,050 --> 00:20:25,680
...your way of sailing is a lot more fun.

375
00:20:26,720 --> 00:20:28,140
Yep, yep.

376
00:20:28,310 --> 00:20:31,470
Hey, why don't you give a pull on that rope?

377
00:20:31,640 --> 00:20:32,850
We're not sailing.

378
00:20:33,020 --> 00:20:36,270
Just pull on it.

379
00:20:33,020 --> 00:20:36,270
All right.

380
00:20:38,360 --> 00:20:40,900
Hey!

381
00:20:38,360 --> 00:20:40,900
Eh?

382
00:20:41,070 --> 00:20:42,860
Sandwiches!

383
00:20:43,030 --> 00:20:45,280
What else?

384
00:20:43,030 --> 00:20:45,280
Ha, ha.

385
00:20:45,570 --> 00:20:47,200
Here you go.

386
00:20:47,370 --> 00:20:50,620
Thank you.

387
00:20:47,370 --> 00:20:50,620
Oh, wow.

388
00:20:53,080 --> 00:20:54,660
What are you doing?

389
00:20:53,080 --> 00:20:54,660
Oops. Sorry.

390
00:20:54,830 --> 00:20:58,000
Don't hold it like that. You're letting all the good stuff fall out.

391
00:20:58,170 --> 00:20:59,920
Oh. Oops.

392
00:20:58,170 --> 00:20:59,920
Careful!

393
00:21:00,090 --> 00:21:02,590
You're wasting good pastrami!

394
00:21:05,470 --> 00:21:08,340
Oh, my God. I'm my dad!

